  outside WRs                        r weeks 1-4 -> 5-17: +0.07 (by season +0.27 +0.20 -0.01 -0.21 +0.13 -0.23 +0.33) | the 4 most extreme defenses keep 13% of their week 1-4 gap
  TEs                                r weeks 1-4 -> 5-17: +0.16 (by season +0.02 +0.07 +0.36 +0.22 +0.07 +0.04 +0.33) | the 4 most extreme defenses keep 20% of their week 1-4 gap
  slot-vs-outside contrast           r weeks 1-4 -> 5-17: +0.11 (by season +0.25 -0.29 +0.03 +0.28 +0.18 +0.31 +0.04) | the 4 most extreme defenses keep 6% of their week 1-4 gap

  read: r near 0 = the 4-week ranking is mostly noise; 'keep' = how much of an extreme team's early gap shows up the rest of the year.

Limitations: PFF alignment shares per player-week (a receiver's points split by his route mix); receiving points only; TE = all TE routes; 2026 = 4 games per defense.
